# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment variables required to run Pulp Ops locally and on Vercel.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the real values.
# .env is git-ignored — never commit credentials.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database (Neon PostgreSQL) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# TWO connection strings are required. Both point to the same Neon database.
# The only difference is the hostname: one routes through Neon's PgBouncer
# pooler, the other connects directly to the Postgres instance.
#
# DATABASE_URL  — pooler endpoint  (hostname contains "-pooler")
#   Used by the running app for all Prisma runtime queries.
#   Supports high connection concurrency via PgBouncer.
#
# DIRECT_URL    — direct endpoint  (hostname has NO "-pooler")
#   Used only by `prisma migrate deploy` / `prisma migrate dev` at build time.
#   Prisma migrations require a PostgreSQL advisory lock, which Neon's pooler
#   does not support. Omitting DIRECT_URL causes a P1002 timeout (or a P1012
#   "variable not found" error) when Vercel runs `prisma migrate deploy`.
#
# How to derive DIRECT_URL from DATABASE_URL — remove "-pooler" from hostname:
#   DATABASE_URL:  ...@ep-example-abc123-pooler.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb...
#   DIRECT_URL:    ...@ep-example-abc123.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb...
#   (user, password, database name, and ?sslmode=require stay identical)
#
# Where to get both strings:
#   Neon Console → your project → Connection Details
#   Choose "Pooled connection"  → DATABASE_URL
#   Choose "Direct connection"  → DIRECT_URL

DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-example-abc123-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-example-abc123.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# ── Vercel deployment checklist ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both variables must be added in Vercel project settings:
#   Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   → Add DATABASE_URL  for Production (+ Preview if used)
#   → Add DIRECT_URL    for Production (+ Preview if used)
#
# A missing DIRECT_URL causes a build failure even when DATABASE_URL is set.
